From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:49:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] phy: airoha: xpon: turn the laser off at shutdown

No driver of the xPON chain (the PHY, the xPON MAC, the EN7570) has a
shutdown callback or a reboot notifier, and the xPON interface going
down keeps the activation alive on purpose. On reboot the laser keeps
answering the OLT's grants until the SoC resets; after a halt or a
power-off, which hang without resetting on this SoC (no pm_power_off),
it keeps transmitting for good.

Add a shutdown callback to the PHY driver that asserts TX_DISABLE and
then the transceiver's VCC_DISABLE, the same states the probe requests
the GPIOs in. The GPIOs go through pinctrl on a MMIO regmap and the
callback runs in process context. A panic is left alone: it resets
within a second (panic_timeout=1), and a notifier taking the pinctrl
lock while another CPU holds it would keep the reset from happening.

Found in the 22-nov-2026 code audit (X1).

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/phy/airoha/phy-airoha-xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/airoha/phy-airoha-xpon.c
@@ -1540,8 +1540,27 @@ static const struct of_device_id airoha_
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, airoha_xpon_phy_of_match);
 
+/*
+ * Nothing else turns the laser off when the system goes down: the GPON MAC
+ * keeps answering the OLT's grants until the SoC resets and, after a halt
+ * or a power-off, which hang without resetting, it keeps doing so for good.
+ * Assert TX_DISABLE first, then cut the transceiver supply. A panic does not
+ * come here; it resets within a second (panic_timeout).
+ */
+static void airoha_xpon_phy_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct airoha_xpon_phy *priv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+
+	if (!priv)
+		return;
+
+	airoha_xpon_phy_set_tx_gpio(priv, false);
+	airoha_xpon_phy_set_vcc_enabled(priv, false);
+}
+
 static struct platform_driver airoha_xpon_phy_driver = {
 	.probe = airoha_xpon_phy_probe,
+	.shutdown = airoha_xpon_phy_shutdown,
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "airoha-xpon-phy",
 		.of_match_table = airoha_xpon_phy_of_match,
